From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] hassio: GA channel bake, GA Supervisor tag, add-on images, full Core

GA deltas of the hassio package (until HAOS 18.x edits of the files
themselves), on HAOS 18.x's containerd/oci-archive bake. Applies after
patches/haos/0003 (armv7 -> OCI arm/v7).

- HASSIO_VERSION_URL ?= GreenAutarky's haos-version (overridable from the make
  command line); installed as /etc/ga-version-url (0444);
- version.json gate: pinned Supervisor/Core, GA Supervisor image,
  check-core-image.sh and check-supervisor-image.sh (GA layer), Supervisor and
  Core equal to the version.yaml pins;
- BR2_PACKAGE_HASSIO_FULL_CORE (Core = homeassistant.<machine>) and
  BR2_PACKAGE_HASSIO_DATA_IMAGE_SIZE;
- add-on images from the board's HASSIO_ADDON_IMAGES_JSON (fetch-addon-images.sh,
  one version file per add-on into fetch-container-image.sh);
- dind import: Supervisor tagged ghcr.io/greenautarky/<arch>-hassio-supervisor:latest;
  the exact image count (images.expected, computed from the inputs) or fail;
- updater.json: channel + baked Core version + Core image;
- GA_HASSIO_SKIP_IMAGES: a board whose arch has no GA image says so, loudly;
  never substituted by an upstream image;
- fetch-container-image.sh: a stale lock the build user cannot write is
  removed before flock.

Not carried from the HAOS 16.3-era edits (obsolete on 18.x): the multi-format
image loader and its online fallback, the registry-auth mount into the dind
container, docker-archive transport, --storage-driver overlay2.
